<title>CANADA: Canada wheat exports to Central America may double.</title>
<headline>Canada wheat exports to Central America may double.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian wheat exports to Central America could double in marketing year 1996/97 (Aug/July) to 150,000 tonnes from 70,000 tonnes in 1995/96, the Canadian Wheat Board said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This is due to the demand for quality wheat in that market and the reduction of U.S. credit subsidies in the area,&quot; the CWB statement said.</p>
<p>Between 1985 and 1995 the CWB exported an annual average of 13,000 tonnes to Guatemala, 6,000 tonnes to El Salvador, 10,000 tonnes to Honduras, 7,000 tonnes to Nicaragua and 1,000 tonnes to Panama, the CWB annual report shows.</p>
</text>
